            <ArticleTitle>Exercise-induced intermittent angina and ST-segment elevation in Prinzmetal's angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with primary angina showed intermittent ST elevation (with and without chest pain), during two exercise tests performed on consecutive days; the same ST changes were also seen during the recovery phase. The electrocardiographic changes recorded in this patient may be considered an example of myocardial response to spasm-related ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
